Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• sector_desc : make sure we only look at “CROPS”.  
• group_desc : pick “FIELD CROPS” for corn and “HORTICULTURE” for mushrooms.  
• commodity_desc : isolate “CORN” and “MUSHROOMS”.  
• statisticcat_desc : keep only rows whose statistic is “PRODUCTION”.  
• unit_desc : production has to be expressed in “BU” (bushels).  
• agg_level_desc : restrict to state‑level data (“STATE”).  
• year : restrict to 2022.  
• value : numeric production figure we finally want.  
• state_alpha / state_name : to label each state in the final output.  

Typical filter block that will be reused  

WHERE year = 2022  
  AND sector_desc = 'CROPS'  
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'  
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'  
  AND value IS NOT NULL  

Below are ten progressive BigQuery statements that explore the data first, then arrive at the combined 2022 corn & mushroom production result.  Every query is limited to 20 rows so they stay short while you explore.

```sql
-- 1.  What years are available in the crops table?
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
ORDER BY year DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  FIELD CROPS: what commodities are recorded as PRODUCTION in 2022?
SELECT DISTINCT commodity_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
ORDER BY commodity_desc
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Check how corn PRODUCTION is expressed (unit codes)
SELECT DISTINCT unit_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
  AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
ORDER BY unit_desc
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Sample rows for corn production in 2022 (bushels only)
SELECT state_alpha, state_name, value, unit_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
  AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND unit_desc = 'BU'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
ORDER BY value DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  HORTICULTURE: verify what units mushrooms are reported in
SELECT DISTINCT unit_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'HORTICULTURE'
  AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
ORDER BY unit_desc
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Sample rows for mushroom production in 2022 (any unit)
SELECT state_alpha, state_name, value, unit_desc
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'HORTICULTURE'
  AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
ORDER BY value DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Total 2022 CORN production by state (bushels)
SELECT
  state_alpha,
  state_name,
  SUM(value) AS corn_bu_2022
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
  AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND unit_desc = 'BU'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
  AND value IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY state_alpha, state_name
ORDER BY corn_bu_2022 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Total 2022 MUSHROOM production by state (bushels if available)
SELECT
  state_alpha,
  state_name,
  SUM(value) AS mushroom_bu_2022
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'HORTICULTURE'
  AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND unit_desc = 'BU'                 -- keep only bushel rows
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
  AND value IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY state_alpha, state_name
ORDER BY mushroom_bu_2022 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Combine corn and mushroom production using UNION ALL
SELECT
  state_alpha,
  state_name,
  'CORN' AS crop,
  SUM(value) AS bu_2022
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
  AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND unit_desc = 'BU'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
  AND value IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY state_alpha, state_name

UNION ALL

SELECT
  state_alpha,
  state_name,
  'MUSHROOMS' AS crop,
  SUM(value) AS bu_2022
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
WHERE year = 2022
  AND group_desc = 'HORTICULTURE'
  AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
  AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
  AND unit_desc = 'BU'
  AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
  AND value IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY state_alpha, state_name
ORDER BY state_alpha, crop
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10.  Final pivot‑style table: each state with both corn and mushroom bushel totals
WITH corn AS (
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, SUM(value) AS corn_bu_2022
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND group_desc = 'FIELD CROPS'
    AND commodity_desc = 'CORN'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND unit_desc = 'BU'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY state_alpha, state_name
),
mush AS (
  SELECT state_alpha, state_name, SUM(value) AS mushroom_bu_2022
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.usda_nass_agriculture.crops`
  WHERE year = 2022
    AND group_desc = 'HORTICULTURE'
    AND commodity_desc = 'MUSHROOMS'
    AND statisticcat_desc = 'PRODUCTION'
    AND unit_desc = 'BU'
    AND agg_level_desc = 'STATE'
    AND value IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY state_alpha, state_name
)
SELECT
  COALESCE(corn.state_alpha, mush.state_alpha)  AS state_alpha,
  COALESCE(corn.state_name , mush.state_name )  AS state_name,
  corn.corn_bu_2022,
  mush.mushroom_bu_2022
FROM corn
FULL OUTER JOIN mush
USING (state_alpha, state_name)
ORDER BY state_alpha
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries take you from quick data inspection all the way to the finished, state‑by‑state 2022 totals for corn and mushroom production in bushels.
